window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-096", "name_zh": "空间/层面", "name_en": "space / planes", "tagline": "没有一个地方真的是空的；分开两个世界的不是距离，是知觉习惯与能量焦点", "explanation": "赛斯说的空间不是那个装东西的空盒子。他说没有一个地方真的是净空的：你身体之外的空间与你身体由同样的材料构成，只是比例不同，两边一直在交换；你甚至会把看起来空着的空间印上你的特色，变成你身体活生生的材料。层面也不是把宇宙叠成几层天花板。它靠的是浓淡与质地：一样东西要达到某个程度、看起来合并成物质，你才感知得到它，而它在别的层面照样确实存在、照样有效。所以分开系统与系统、分开你与或然实相、分开你与死后的人的，不是空间也不是时间，而是感知的习惯与能量的焦点；不在那个层面，就等于不在那里，中间只隔着一层不觉察的面纱。赛斯为什么要给这套坐标：因为你对实相的观念有多狭窄，自我就多努力把你留在那个小世界里；而成长真正的意思不是占据更大的空间，是值与性质的扩展。看清这套坐标，梦、出体、想象、甚至死亡，都不再是从这里走到那里，而是焦点换个方向。", "definitions": [{"zh": "在你深入挖掘自己之际，你会发现其他实相的蛛丝马迹。在你们称之为物质宇宙的同一个空间内，你们的系统并不是唯一存在的系统。你们根本没有感知到这些其他的系统。区隔一个系统与另一个系统时，并不是空间或时间。然而，感知习惯却将它们一分为二。", "en": "As you dig deeper into yourself you will find hints of other realities. Yours is not the only system that exists within what you would call the same space as the physical universe. You simply do not perceive these other systems. It is not space or time that divides one system from another. Habits of perception divide them however.", "source": "Session 248"}, {"zh": "其实每件以实质出现的东西也存在于你所不能感知的方式里。只当实物达到某一个“程度”，当它们似乎合并成物质时，你才会感知到它们。但它们在别的层面确实存在而且有效。", "en": "Now anything that appears in physical terms also exists in other terms that you do not perceive. You only perceive realities when they achieve a certain “pitch,” when they seem to coalesce into matter. But they actually exist, and quite validly at other levels.", "source": "Session 530"}, {"zh": "这里我有几件事情要讨论。我已经讲过的可能实相与你自己的实相，并不是在空间上，而是在能量焦点上，是分开的。你们所谓死后犹存的人格与你们也不是在空间上，而是在能量焦点上，是分开的。 你在身体上感知不到他们。它们的焦点已经改变了方向。就可能的实相而言，能量的焦点向来不同于你自己的实相。你应该知道，在某些状况下，与死后犹存的人格接触是很有可能的。但是，对你来说，与你自己的可能人格接触却是非常困难。", "en": "I have a few matters to discuss here. The probable realities of which I have spoken are separated from your own, not in terms of space but in terms of energy focus. Survival personalities, as you term them, are not separated from you in space either, but in terms of energy focus.You do not perceive them physically. The direction of focus for them has changed. In the case of probable realities the focus of energy has always been different from your own. It is quite possible, as you should know, under certain circumstances, to contact survival personalities. It is highly difficult however for you to contact your own probable personalities.", "source": "Session 310"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "没有一个地方真的是空的", "note": "第329节这句话可以当这一页的钥匙：去看看什么都没有的地方，因为没有一个地方真的是净空的；看着像空的地方反而没有扭曲，看着满满的空间才骗人，因为那里的实相已经被压成一个僵化的形式。第2节把这件事落到你自己身上——你布置一个房间时在给它按下你的印记，同时也把看来空着的那部分变成你身体活生生的材料，而你根本没意识到自己在做。第614节说得更具体：身体之外那个空间，构成它的材料与你身体相同，只是比例不一样，两边每时每刻在做实质交换，没有这种交换就没有生命。第240、244节则把「在空间里的位置」本身说成一种协议、一种大家都同意的连贯性。第888节挑明结论：时间与空间每一件都是心理属性的结果。", "src": "第 329、2、614、240、244、888 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 329 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 2 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 614 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 240 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 244 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 888 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-096-e1151", "zh": "这些问题有很多在我们的课当中讨论过，现在没有时间告诉你们。去看看什么都没有的地方，因为没有一个地方真的是净空的。在看起来什么都没有的地方，不会有扭曲。在那表面的虚无之内，如果你知道怎么看的话，实相就能够显现。那看起来满满的，那看起来满满的空间，是令人误解的，因为实相已经被赋予了一个僵化的形式。", "en": "Many of these we have discussed in our sessions, and there is no time now to tell you. Look where nothing seems to be, for no place is truly empty. Where there appears to be nothing, there will be no distortion. Within that seeming nothingness, reality can show itself if you know how to look. That which appears full, that space which appears full, is misleading, for reality is already given to a rigid form.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第329节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "329", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2653", "zh": "很明显的，当你装修一个房间时，你以你的特色铭记它，但你也以同样的方式，印记（停顿良久）看来仿佛是空的空间——那是说，你将空的空间变成你身体活生生的物质，而根本从未认识到你在这样做。你的健康与日常的天气彼此互动。这发生在一个个人的和集体的基础上。我承认，这些资料某部分相当与你们平常的概念相左，但你身体的健康不只是密切地与世界的健康相关，却也与物质的气候相关。", "en": "It is obvious that you impress a room with your characteristics as you furnish it, but you also mark (long pause) what seems to be empty space in the same fashion — that is, you turn empty space into the living matter of your body without ever realizing that you do so. Your health and the daily weather interact with each other. This happens on a personal and mass basis. I admit that some of this material quite contradicts your usual ideas, but the health of your body is intimately related not only to the state of world health, but to the physical climate as well.", "source": "健康之道 · 第2节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "2", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1790", "zh": "在你身体之外的“空间”，其基本构成的材料与组成你身体的材料相同，有所不同的只是“比例”而已。这个“空间”与那个你称它为“身体”的东西之间，有着持续不断的各种实质的“交换”行为在发生，这种互换包括了化学的交互作用以及各种基本的交换。若无这种互换，你们所谓的“生命”根本就不可能存在。", "en": "The stuff, the space outside of your body, is composed of the same elements, but in different proportions. There is a constant physical interchange between the structure you call your body and the space outside it; chemical interactions, basic exchanges without which life as you know it would be impossible.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第614节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "614", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1009", "zh": "我告诉过你，每一个个体都会创造实体物质，包括物体在内，也说过他会建构自己的肉体形象。连贯性、永久不变的幻相、在空间的位置、颜色与质量，这些全部都以我已经清楚解释过的方式达成协议。（在第二册，见1964年夏天给出的第60至73节，以及其他很多节。）", "en": "I have told you that each individual creates physical matter, including objects, that he constructs his own physical image. Coherence, the illusion of permanency, placement in space, color and mass, all these are arrived at and agreed upon, in ways that I have clearly explained. （In Volume 2, see the 60th to 73rdsessions, given during the summer of1964, plus many others.）", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第240节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "240", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1022", "zh": "因为我已经解释过的其他程序，包括持续心电感应的存在，所以关于这些物体在空间中的定位，或者如果鲁柏更喜欢的话，就说地点，是存在某种协议的。现在这引发了你可以称之为质量－感知（mass-perception）的东西，两个词之间使用连字符。", "en": "Because of other procedures which I have explained, including hiding the existence of constant telepathy, there is some agreement as to the placement of these objects, or if Ruburt prefers, locations, in space. Now this gives rise to what you may call mass-perception, with a hyphen between the two words.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第244节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "244", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2496", "zh": "你们无法给宇宙的开始精确定位——因为（突然较大声）那个开始同时也是太大和太小，不能被含容在你们任何明确的陈述里。虽然在那些明确的陈述里，每件事都干净利落，而且完整。你们在时间与空间的戏院里，实在是以无比漫不经心的方式在运作的。时间和空间，每件都是心理属性的结果。（停顿。）当你们问宇宙有多老，或世界有多老时，那时你们已经确认时间和空间多少是几乎绝对的性质。你们的问题是，只有走出通常经验的范围之外，才能找到答案——因为在那经验之内，你们总是被带回到开始和结束，顺序而来的时刻和其内似无其它来源的证据的一个世界。", "en": "You cannot pinpoint the beginning of the universe—for (suddenly louder) that beginning is simultaneously too vast and too small to be contained in any of your specifications. While everything seems neat and tidy within those specifications, and whole, you operate with brilliant nonchalance in the theater of time and space. Time and space are each the result of psychological properties. (Pause.) When you ask how old is the universe, or how old is the world, then you are taking it for granted that time and space are somehow or other almost absolute qualities. You are asking for answers that can only be found by going outside of the context of usual experience—for within that experience you are always led back to beginnings and endings, consecutive moments, and a world that seems to have within it no evidences of any other source.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第888节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "888", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "你所在的同一块空间里，并排着别的系统", "note": "第248节是全页最清楚的一段：在你称之为物质宇宙的同一个空间内，你们的系统并不是唯一存在的系统，你根本没有感知到那些系统；把一个系统与另一个系统分开的，不是空间也不是时间，而是感知的习惯。第258节把它压成一句：其他系统就在你自己系统占的同一块空间里。第248节另一段说它们共存却不能自然相遇，就像负宇宙与你的宇宙共存却被分开。第489节提醒，你们连自己这套系统里的生命形态都没分完，有许多同居者你永远无法在物质上知觉到，连你自己的思想形体你也跟不出自家门。第118节说这些场域和层面比你所能想象的还多，那边的居民常常只是碰巧收到了你们的频道，而他们对你们存在的觉知并不比你们对他们的更多。第29节更直接：前面提过的层面没有一个觉察到你们的层面。第903节补一句——在你们认知的那个地球存在之前，同样的空间里就有过别的地球。", "src": "第 248、258、489、118、29、903 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 248 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 258 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 489 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 118 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 29 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 903 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-096-e1026", "zh": "在你深入挖掘自己之际，你会发现其他实相的蛛丝马迹。在你们称之为物质宇宙的同一个空间内，你们的系统并不是唯一存在的系统。你们根本没有感知到这些其他的系统。区隔一个系统与另一个系统时，并不是空间或时间。然而，感知习惯却将它们一分为二。", "en": "As you dig deeper into yourself you will find hints of other realities. Yours is not the only system that exists within what you would call the same space as the physical universe. You simply do not perceive these other systems. It is not space or time that divides one system from another. Habits of perception divide them however.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第248节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "248", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1043", "zh": "其他系统存在你们自己的系统占用的相同空间之内，但你无法感知它们。", "en": "Other systems exist within the same space occupied by your own, but you cannot perceive them.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第258节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "258", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1029", "zh": "他们会认为你们自己的系统是一个可能的宇宙。你们会做梦，他们也会做梦。你们利用原子和分子，他们也是。系统是分开的，但不是被空间或时间分开。它们共存但却不能自然相遇，正如负宇宙与你们自己的宇宙共存，但却与它分开。", "en": "They would consider your own system as a probable universe. They dream as you dream. They utilize atoms and molecules as you do. The systems are divided, but not separated by space or time. They coexist but they cannot meet naturally, as the negative universe coexists with your own but is divided from it.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第248节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "248", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1339", "zh": "即便在物质层面，你们也还没有把所有的生命形态分门别类；在你们的系统里，有许多同居的生命是你们永远无法在物质上知觉到的。你们也不理解自己的思想、自己的思想形体所具有的多重实相；你们无法跟着它们走出你们自己的心智之家。", "en": "Even physically you have not categorized all of the life-forms, and there are many co-inhabiting your system that you will never physically perceive. You do not understand the multiple reality of your own thoughts or thought forms, and you are not able to follow them out of your own mental home.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第489节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "489", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0744", "zh": "这些场域和层面之多样，超过你们所能想像的，而且它们的形成，基本上，方式和你们自己的宇宙一样，那些居民有很多自发又颇为意外地收听着你们的宇宙。但大部分这类层面上的居民对你们的实际存在，并没有比你们对他们的存在更有觉知。", "en": "These fields or planes are more various than you can imagine, and they are formed in the same manner, basically, as your own universe was formed, and many of those inhabitants tune in on your universe spontaneously and quite accidentally. But the inhabitants of most such planes are no more aware of your actual existence than you are of their existence.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第118节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "118", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0230", "zh": "前面提过的层面没有一个觉察到你们的层面。除了已建立文化的存在之外，其中还有另外的类别，这些类别尽量不用伪装模式，而且也不像已建立文化的存在和你们自己的层面那么相似。这些类别只有在某些要表达和处理尚未化解的内在冲突时，才会将伪装模式具体化。这件事我还不想讲得这么深入，因为可能会让人混淆。", "en": "None of the above mentioned are aware of your plane. There is among others another classification beside culture establishment existences, and these keep camouflage patterns at a minimum and are not as similar as cultural establishment existences are to your own plane. These materialize camouflage pattern only at certain times to express and deal with inner conflicts not yet worked out. I did not intend to get into this so deeply yet, as it may be confusing to say the least.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第29节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "29", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2544", "zh": "当你问：“世界是什么时候开始的？”或“真的发生了什么？”或“是否有一个伊甸园？”你是在指如你所了解的世界。但以那种说法，在你们认知的地球存在之前，在同样的空间就有地球存在过，而它们是以本书前面的章节里我告诉你们的方式开始的。地球的模式在你们的时间次元里继续，虽然，在那个时间次元里那些世界必须消失，以便继续“它们在时间外的存在”。那些模式又被填满了。", "en": "When you ask: “When did the world begin?” or “What really happened?” or “Was there a Garden of Eden?”, you are referring to the world as you understand it, but in those terms there were earths in the same space before the earth you recognize existed,2 and they began in the manner that I have given you in the early chapters of this book. The patterns for worlds—the patterns—continue in your time dimension, though in that time dimension those worlds must disappear, again, to continue “their existence outside of time.” The patterns are filled out again.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第903节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "903", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "层面按频率和强度分，不是一层层的天花板", "note": "这一块的要点是别让「层面」这个词骗出叠楼房的画面。第530节给了真正的判据：一样东西要达到某个程度、看起来合并成物质了，你才感知得到它；它在别的层面照样确实存在而且有效。所以层面的分别更接近浓淡、质地、频率，而不是上下。第289节说一个经验由电磁脉冲组成，里面有一种与空间毫无关系的深度，它的存在靠的是强度而不是持续时间。第302节把这条推到你身上：从全我的内核朝四面八方飞出去的形象与物件，那种冲力与动向是强度上的，不是空间里的。第125节说电子系统里没有就空间或时间而言的距离。第79节说意念能量在别的层面被觉察到，而它转换成物质场那一段反而没被觉察。第16节留了个有意思的尾巴：同一个层面，对法兰克·沃茨而言是个悲伤的层面。", "src": "第 530、289、302、125、79、16 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 530 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 289 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 302 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 125 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 79 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 16 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-096-e1433", "zh": "其实每件以实质出现的东西也存在于你所不能感知的方式里。只当实物达到某一个“程度”，当它们似乎合并成物质时，你才会感知到它们。但它们在别的层面确实存在而且有效。", "en": "Now anything that appears in physical terms also exists in other terms that you do not perceive. You only perceive realities when they achieve a certain “pitch,” when they seem to coalesce into matter. But they actually exist, and quite validly at other levels.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第530节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "530", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1087", "zh": "一个经验大致上是由电磁脉冲组成的它们包含一种深度，与空间一点关系都没有，一种依赖——再一次——强度而不是持续时间长度的存在。然而，因为你自己的基本假设，这样的经验，被内在感知到，以行经种种强度的方式重播，因而在你们自己的维度内产生了一趟时间之旅。", "en": "An experience in general is composed of electromagnetic pulsations. (Long pause) They contain a kind of depth, having nothing to do with space, an existence dependent upon, again, intensity rather than duration. However, because of your own basic assumptions such experiences, perceived by the inner senses, are played back in such a manner that a traveling through intensities results in a journey through time within your own dimension. I believe it will be found that differences will occur in the plus and minus charges in the body during such episodes.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第289节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "289", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1110", "zh": "肉体形象是客观实相的一部分。说到自己的时候，不应该忽略这一点。一方面，肉体形象和实质物体从全我的内在核心朝着四面八方飞出去。冲力、行动和动向一直都有；也就是说，在强度上，而不是空间里。", "en": "The physical image is a part of objective reality. This should not be overlooked, when speaking of the self. In one respect the physical image and physical objects go flying out in all directions from the inner core of the whole self. There is always impetus, action, and motion; that is, of intensities and not of space.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第302节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "302", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0762", "zh": "在电子系统里，也没有就空间或时间而言的距离。", "en": "Nor, in the electrical system, is there distance in terms of space or time.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第125节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "125", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0625", "zh": "本身由能量组成的意念，被转化或转换成其他的能量类型，你们碰巧可以在许多情形中察觉到它。在其他层面上，意念能量是被觉察的，而能量转换进入物质层面则没有被察觉到。", "en": "Ideas, being themselves composed of energy, are translated or transformed into other kinds of energy, which you happen in many instances to perceive. On other planes the idea energy is perceived, and the energy transformed into physical fields is not perceived.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第79节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "79", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0092", "zh": "法兰克·沃茨确实来自悲伤的状态。他是一个重修的人格，也就是说，我必须透过法兰克·沃茨弥补过去的错误。这从来不是一个漂亮的议题。这些似乎在一站又一站的悲伤流转的人，通常都是这一类型。我不应该轻视法兰克·沃茨，因为他几乎可以说是我的救赎。这个层面对法兰克·沃茨而言是个悲伤的层面。我当然会完全补偿他，或尝试这样做。他一点幽默感都没有。", "en": "Frank Watts did indeed come from the state of sorrow. He was a makeup personality—that is, through Frank Watts I had to make up for past errors. Never a pretty proposition. These people who seem borne from sorrow to sorrow are often of this type. I should not make light of Frank Watts, since almost literally he redeemed me. This plane for Frank Watts was a plane of sorrow. I will of course make it all up to him, or try to. He has absolutely no sense of humor.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第16节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "16", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "不在那个层面，就等于不在那里", "note": "第310节是这一页最要紧的一句：或然实相与你的实相、你们所谓死后犹存的人格与你们，都不是在空间上分开，而是在能量的焦点上分开；它们的焦点换了方向，所以你在身体上感知不到它们。于是第97节说，隔开你和另一个你的、隔开两个场域或层面的，只不过是不觉察这块面纱。第671节冷冷地补一句：这个空间本来就不是同一个，只对你显得是同一个。第515节特别说明赛斯讲的距离不是空间的距离。第260节划出界线：心智上你可以穿越空间，肉体上不能，而他谈维度时指的不是空间系统。第43节把话说到底：穿过空间的移动本身就是一种扭曲，所以第八种内在感官解套才那么重要。第716节给了实用版：把焦点从你组织好的实相挪开，你没贯注的那一部分自己会跑到你面前来。", "src": "第 310、97、671、515、260、43、716 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 310 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 97 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 671 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 515 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 260 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 43 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 716 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-096-e1127", "zh": "这里我有几件事情要讨论。我已经讲过的可能实相与你自己的实相，并不是在空间上，而是在能量焦点上，是分开的。你们所谓死后犹存的人格与你们也不是在空间上，而是在能量焦点上，是分开的。 你在身体上感知不到他们。它们的焦点已经改变了方向。就可能的实相而言，能量的焦点向来不同于你自己的实相。你应该知道，在某些状况下，与死后犹存的人格接触是很有可能的。但是，对你来说，与你自己的可能人格接触却是非常困难。", "en": "I have a few matters to discuss here. The probable realities of which I have spoken are separated from your own, not in terms of space but in terms of energy focus. Survival personalities, as you term them, are not separated from you in space either, but in terms of energy focus.You do not perceive them physically. The direction of focus for them has changed. In the case of probable realities the focus of energy has always been different from your own. It is quite possible, as you should know, under certain circumstances, to contact survival personalities. It is highly difficult however for you to contact your own probable personalities.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第310节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "310", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0698", "zh": "你忘记了在广阔的现在，你已经不是你将会是，而是你已经是的你。因此，你要投射的这类人格已经被投射了，分隔你的只不过是毫无觉察的这层面纱而已，就像分开两个场域或层面的只不过是毫无觉察的这层面纱一样。", "en": "You forget that in the spacious present you already are not only what you will be, but what you have been. Therefore, such personalities that you would project are already projected, and only the veil of unawareness divides you, as only the veil of unawareness ever separates one field or plane from another.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第97节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "97", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1945", "zh": "无论如何，这个空间并不是同一个，也不是同样的。它只对你显得是如此罢了。", "en": "(Very intently:) The space is not the same, or identical, in any case. It only appears to be so to you.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第671节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "671", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1403", "zh": "在某方面来说它也与我自己的环境有距离，因为在我自己的环境里，把资料以偏向物质化的术语加以说明，对我而言会有些困难，你们必须了解这距离并不是指空间的距离。", "en": "It is also in a way distant from my own environment, for in my own environment I would have some difficulties in relating information in physically oriented terms. You must understand that by distance I do not refer to space.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第515节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "515", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1050", "zh": "当然，进行其他维度和系统的心智或心灵之旅是可能的，当我谈到维度时，我指的不是空间系统。心智上，你可以穿越空间，但肉体上，你不能。在你的一些梦状态中，你的确行经其他维度和其他系统。这些梦中旅行的范围取决于你自己的能力。", "en": "Of course mental or psychic journeys into other dimensions and systems are possible, and when I speak of dimensions here I am not referring to space systems. Mentally you can cut through space, physically you cannot. In some of your dream states you do travel through other dimensions and other systems. The extent of these dream travels is determined by your own ability.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第260节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "260", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0385", "zh": "穿过空间的移动是一种扭曲，我期望在今后的课程上对此作更多的说明，，因为它非常重要；也许你们现在或许可以看出我们的第八种内在感官，解套，为什么这么重要了，因为内我必须在它能改变之前从一种特殊的伪装中摆脱（disentangle）出来。可以这样说，它必须忽略一套伪装，能够顺利地采用另一套，或者干脆彻底去除伪装。", "en": "The movement through space is a distortion. I expect to say much more about this in further sessions, as it is extremely important; and you can see now perhaps why our eighth sense, disentanglement, is so important, since the inner self must disentangle itself from a particular camouflage before it can change. It must ignore, so to speak, one set of camouflage and be able to either adopt another smoothly or to dispense with camouflage entirely.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第43节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "43", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2159", "zh": "在你们的本台里，事件是清楚的在空间与时间里被碰到的。可是，当你挪开时，你可能在时间里，却非在空间里碰到事件，而你曾试图否认的实相于是可能生动的出现。如果你了解这点，你就会受用不尽，因为当你把你的焦点由你组织好的实相移开时，你没有贯注其上的其它部分就会跑到你面前来。", "en": "In your home station, events are encountered clearly in space and time. When you move away, however, you may meet events in time but not in space, and reality that you have tried to deny may then appear vividly. If you understand this you can gain immeasurably, for as you move your focus away from your organized reality, other portions of it upon which you have not concentrated will come into view.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第716节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "716", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "你被配到哪一层，就看到哪一层的世界", "note": "第15节立了规矩：感官依据物质化的层面而改变。赛斯自己可以在限度之内换形态，而换形态不是把自己的样子改掉，是选择成为别的东西的一部分。第96节立刻推出一个后果：内在资料要透过内在感官来感知，而任何一个既定实相层面专属的那套外在感官配备都会把它扭曲，人照自己的形象造自己的神，就是这么回事。第291节说明为什么这一层看不见那一层：自我几乎完全由肉体感官的感知方法塑成，那套更古老、更宽、限制也更少的机制它用不了，而自己的其他层面在生理上仍然会对它们起反应。第571节给了读法：象征可以当成你在意识各层面知觉方式的路标，梦里出现真的火，就明白你正在用调准到肉体的意识感知实相。第211节解释为什么这几层互相不知道：人格的所有层面确实都是意识的层面，只是按隔间的方式运作。", "src": "第 15、96、291、571、211 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 15 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 96 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 291 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 571 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 211 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-096-e0069", "zh": "我之前说过，感官依据物质化的层面而改变。如果你说的是我现在的形态，那我可以是很多不同的形态。也就是说，我可以在有限的方式内，改变自己的状态，但在这样做的过程中，我实际上并没有改变我的形态，而是选择成为其他东西的一部分。", "en": "As I have mentioned earlier the senses change according to the plane of materialization. If you are speaking about my present form, I can be many forms. That is, within limits I can change my form, but in doing so I do not actually change my form so much as I choose to become part of something else.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第15节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "15", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0688", "zh": "如你所知，内在资料( inner data）必须透过内在感官感知。在制定有关原始能量完形的一个理论时，这些资料被任何既定实相层面特有的专属外在感官配备所扭曲。大家知道，人们按照他自己的形象创造他的上帝。", "en": "As you know, inner data must be perceived through the inner senses. In formulating a theory concerning the primary energy gestalt, the data is distorted by the peculiar set of outer sensory equipment characteristic of any given plane of reality. This is known, that man forms his god in his own image.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第96节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "96", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1093", "zh": "然而，另一种比较古老的感知机制依然存留。自我没有也无法利用它们。事实上，自我几乎完全是由肉体感官的感知方法所形成的。自己的其他层面在生理上回应着比较古老、比较广泛但也比较没有限制的感知机制。", "en": "The other, older perceptive mechanisms still linger on however. The ego does not and cannot make use of them. Indeed the ego is almost entirely formed by the physical senses method of perception. Other layers of the self biologically respond to the older, more generalized but less limited perceptive mechanisms.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第291节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "291", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1522", "zh": "到某个程度，所有这些都是你的意识的流动性以及它能很容易的被利用的小例子。以一种奇怪的方式，象征可以被看成是你在意识的各种不同层面的“知觉方式”的实例。它们变换的扮相可以作为路标。例如，火是一个具体化了的象征，因此一个真的火显然告诉你，你是在以你调整到肉体的意识去感知实相。", "en": "To some extent, all of these are small examples of the mobility of your consciousness, and the ease with which it can be used. In a strange manner, symbols can be regarded as samples of the way you perceive at various levels of consciousness. Their changing guises can be used as signposts. Fire, for example, is a symbol made physical, so a real fire tells you obviously that you are perceiving reality with your physically attuned consciousness.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第571节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "571", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0941", "zh": "人格所有层面都确实是意识的层面。它们仅以区隔的方式来运作，因此自己的一部分常常并不觉察自己的其他部分。通常当你醒着的时候，你不知道睡着时的自己；你对你的邻居还比较了解，因此你睡着时的自己实际上仍然是很神秘的。当你醒着的时候，就像鲁柏写下的，你无法找到仅一个晚上之前你还很熟悉的梦中地点。", "en": "All layers of the personality are indeed conscious layers. They simply operate in the manner of compartments, so that often one portion of the self is not aware of other portions. As a rule when you are awake you do not know your sleeping self; you know your neighbors far better, so your sleeping self appears mysterious indeed. When you are awake, as Ruburt himself has written, you cannot find the dream locations that have been so familiar to you only the night before.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第211节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "211", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "真正的扩展不占空间", "note": "第44节把两套成长摆在一起：在你们的宇宙里，成长常常意味着占据更多空间；在赛斯说的内在宇宙里，成长是值与性质的扩展，不意味着任何一种空间扩展，也不意味着像你们那样投射进时间。第54节顺势改写宇宙扩展论——你们的宇宙确实在扩展，但不是就空间、也不是就时间而言，而是就能力与价值完成而言，你现在存在的这一层只是其中之一。第73节用一幅画做比方：那幅画的元素以同样方式扩展，它与空间无关，只有价值完成，它有自己的深度与视角，不只在物质建构的背面，也在建构的内部。第250节解释了为什么你想不通：你们被开始与结束催眠得太深，硬要把这个概念接上你们看到的宇宙时就撞墙了，因为你以为在外面看到的确实就是空间。第565节把灵魂本身说成一种多重空间的无量行动，因着这无边的行动为自己造出无尽的空间。", "src": "第 44、54、73、250、565 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 44 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 54 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 73 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 250 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 565 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-096-e0402", "zh": "在你们的伪装宇宙内，成长往往意味着占据更多的空间。事实上，在我们实相的内在宇宙中，成长存在我说过的值或性质的扩展之内，而且没有，我再重复一遍，没有意味着任何一种空间扩展的意思。它也没有意味着，像你们伪装宇宙的成长那样，一种进入时间的投射。", "en": "Growth in your camouflage universe often involves the taking up of more space. Actually in our inner universe of reality growth exists in terms of the value or quality expansion of which I have spoken, and does not, I repeat, does not imply any sort of space expansion. Nor does it imply, as growth does in your camouflage universe, a sort of projection into time.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0471", "zh": "在它之内，没有你们以为的过去、现在或将来，只有现在。因为在这个现在之内有无止无尽的可能性，所以耐久性被维持着，就价值完成、真的无止无尽的价值完成而言。于是，这座森林不断扩展。记得你们的宇宙扩展论，但不是就空间，或其实是时间来说，而是就在可能被建构在各个层面上以及各种伪装中的能力与价值完成而言，你们目前存在的层面就是其中一个。", "en": "There is no past, present or future in your terms within it, but only a now. Because of the endless possibilities within this now, durability is maintained in terms of value fulfillment, the fulfillment of literally endless values. Therefore the forest is constantly expanding. Remember your expanding universe theory, but not in terms of space or indeed in terms of time, but in terms of fulfillment of abilities and values that may be constructed upon various levels and in various guises, your present plane of existence being one.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第54节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "54", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0608", "zh": "检查画的背面不会有任何东西。这幅画的元素会以我曾告诉你们的宇宙扩展的方式来扩展，它与空间毫无关系，有的只是价值完成，它有自己的深度和视角，不仅仅存在于物质建构的背后，同时也存在架构之内。", "en": "Examination of the back of the painting would show nothing. The elements of the painting would expand in the same way that I have told you the universe expands, in a way that has nothing to do with space but of value fulfillment, which has its own kind of depth and perspective, and which exists not only behind but within the construction of matter.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第73节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "73", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1033", "zh": "只是因为你们被开始和结束的观念催眠了，所以坚持在宇宙中搜寻它们，而扭曲了对你们来说本来清楚可见的资料。我告诉过你，宇宙以一种与空间无关的方式扩展。但是，当你们试图把这个概念与你们所知的宇宙连结在一起时，你们会发现自己正对着一面砖墙，因为你们在宇宙中好像看到的其实是空间。", "en": "It is only because you are so hypnotized with ideas of beginning and endings that you persist in searching for them in the universe, and you distort data that would otherwise be clear to you. I have told you that the universe expands in a way that has nothing to do with space. But when you try to relate this idea to the universe as you know it, you find yourself up against a brick wall, for what you seem to see out in the universe is indeed space.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第250节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "250", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1731", "zh": "若以活动来形容灵魂，我们可说灵魂的本身就是一种多重空间性无量行动的组合，它的每一个微小的可能都已实现，也都已存在，由于这种无量无边的行动，它为自己造出了无尽的空间以完成它“自我圆满”的追求。", "en": "The soul can be described for that matter, as a multidimensional, infinite act, each minute probability being brought somewhere into actuality and existence; an infinite creative act that creates for itself infinite dimensions in which fulfillment is possible.", "source": "时空之外 · 第565节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "565", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "你本来就在许多层面同时在场", "note": "第40节的比方很好用：蜘蛛织它的网，它的建构被严格限在一个层面；你不是，你可能同时在许多层面都有实相产生，而且用的方式你自己还不熟。第58节把范围放大到一个存有：它可以存在于许多不同的层面，带着先前所有层面的知识，它的每一个外在自我都有相同的机会。第722节给了个让人一愣的说法：你所知的自己，是一个从未真正出现的原始自己在时间与空间里的物质性痕迹或侵入，所以从某种说法上，你跟电子一样像鬼影。第704节说那个内在多次元的自己基本上在时空之外，同时却让你能在时空之内运作。第740节呼应：所谓的灵魂与空间时间里的大小或久暂没有关连，只限于它与之结合去体验的那些范畴。第521节和第894节把设计讲完——你只因此刻焦点在这一角，就把整个存在等同于它，而那个高度集中的实质自己需要被独立于时空之外的知识领域支持着。", "src": "第 40、58、722、704、740、521、894 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 40 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 58 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 722 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 704 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 740 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 521 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 894 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-096-e0322", "zh": "你们建构你们的伪装存在，就如同蜘蛛织它的网一样，可是你们却不会觉察到丝线的奥秘。虽然卑微的蜘蛛编织着它的网子时，你们很容易会心一笑，但并不了解这些丝线是在你们自己里面产生的。蜘蛛的建构被严格地限定在一个层面，而你们的建构则不是，你们可能在许多层面立刻会有实相产生，产生的方式你们自己也不熟悉。", "en": "You construct your own camouflage existence as the spider constructs his web, but you are not aware of the threads. You do not understand that they originate within yourself, although it is very simple to smile as the lowly spider weaves its web. The spiders construction is severely limited to one plane, but this is not the case with your constructions, which may have reality on many planes at once, and in ways with which you are not familiar.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第40节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "40", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0522", "zh": "所以在它之内的确包含它在你们层面上有过经验的知识，虽然这样一个存有可能从任何层面跳出来。这当然代表最不寻常的可能性，而且这样的一个存有，如果被它本身的力量驱策的话，可以存在许多不同的层面，带着先前所有层面的知识；并且它的每一个外在自我都有相同的机会。这很重要。", "en": "It does therefore contain within it the knowledge of its experiences upon your plane, though such an entity can spring from any plane. This of course represents the most extraordinary possibility, and such an entity can, if it is so propelled by its own strength, exist upon a variety of planes, carrying along with it knowledge of all previous planes; and each of its outer egos have the same opportunities. This is important.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2184", "zh": "不过，基本上，这样一个粒子的每个“显现”都是一个自己版本（self-version），因为它多少被它自己的“位置”改变了。人类的“自己”也可以同时出现在几个地方，每一个这种出现微妙的改变了那“人类的”粒子，所以，每一个出现都是“原始”自己的一个版本，而以那种说法，原始自己从不以它自己的样子在别处出现。当你看着一个电子——假设你看得到——你是在观察一个全然不同的东西之痕迹或路径，而那出现被称为一个电子。所以，你所知的自己是一个从未出现的“原始自己”在时间与空间里的一个物质性痕迹或侵入。那么，以一种说法，你跟电子一样的像鬼影。", "en": "Basically, however, each “appearance” of such a particle is a self-version, for it is altered to some extent by its “location.” Period. So can the human self appear in several places at once,5 each such appearance subtly altering the “human” particle, so that each appearance is a version of an “original” self that as itself never appears in those terms.6 When you look at an electron — figuratively speaking — you are observing a trace or a track of something else entirely, and that appearance is termed an electron. So the self that you know is a physical trace or intrusion into space and time of an “original” self that never appears. In a way, then, you are as ghostly as an electron.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第722节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "722", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2072", "zh": "且说，所有这些对许多人而言显然听起来很不科学，然而，我大多数的读者早已经认识了一种不同版本的科学本质，不然，他们一开始就不会在看这本书了。内在神谕：那是什么意思？它与未知的实相有什么关系？更有进者，它与实际的世界又有什么关系？内在神谕是内在多次元自己的声音——这内在的自己即是每个人的那个不完全涵括在他个人性之内的部分，未知的“自己结构”的那部分，个人性及其“肉体性的联盟”由其中跃出。基本上，心灵的那个部分是在时间与空间之外的，同时却使你能在其内运作，它密切的与可能性打交道，而那是所有可预测的行动之泉源。", "en": "Now all of this certainly sounds unscientific to many people, yet most of my readers have already picked up a different version of the nature of science, or they would not be reading this book to begin with. The private oracle: What does that mean? And what does it have to do with the unknown reality? More, what does it have to do with the practical world? The private oracle is the voice of the inner multidimensional self — the part of each person not fully contained in his or her personhood, the part of the unknown self-structure out of which personhood, with its physical alliance, springs. Basically that portion of the psyche is outside of space and time, while enabling you to operate in it.4 It deals intimately with probabilities — (louder:) the source of all predictable action.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第704节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "704", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2235", "zh": "所谓的灵魂与在空间与时间里的大小或久暂并无关联，除了在那些范畴里它们与之结合以体验的之外。", "en": "The soul, so-called, is not related to size or duration in space and time, except insofar as it is wedded to experience within those contexts.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第740节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "740", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1665", "zh": "多重空间性的“我”同时扮演着众多角色，创造了这些“宇宙激情剧”，自己也参与演出。因为你目前只把焦点集中在这一角色上，就认为这个角色是全部的自己。当然你为自己设下各种规则及限制是有原因的，意识既是处于一种蕴蓄变化的状态之中，我说的这个多重空间性的“我”便不是一个已经完成的心理结构，它也是存在与一种蕴蓄变化的状态之中。", "en": "You are the multidimensional self who has these existences, who creates and takes part in these cosmic passion plays, so to speak. It is only because you focus in this particular role now that you identify your entire being with it. You have set these rules for yourself for a reason. And consciousness is in a state of becoming, and so this multidimensional self of which I speak is not a psychological structure completed and done with. It is also in a state of becoming.", "source": "时空之外 · 第521节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "521", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2528", "zh": "所需要的是可以在一个时空架构里有效运作的一个高度集中及精确对准的实质自己，那个架构是与实质生物一同形成的——不过，那个自己却多少必须被某种基本上独立于时空之外的信息和知识领域所支持。一个不可或缺却也不被允许去使实质焦点偏离的知识。", "en": "What was needed was a highly focused, precisely tuned physical self that could operate efficiently in a space and time scheme that was being formed along with physical creatures—a self, however, that in one way or another must be supported by realms of information and knowledge of a kind that was basically independent of time and space. A knowledge indispensable, and yet a knowledge that could not be allowed to distract the physical focus.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第894节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "894", "only_en": true}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "梦与出体：走不了距离的那一段，改换层面", "note": "这一页跟梦那几页的分工是：那边讲梦的内容，这边讲梦提供了另一套坐标。第219节说，在梦的状态里，自我从时间是一串片刻这个概念里被放出来，自己的其他部分就能走过这些片刻点，开始一趟与你的时空概念无关的、穿越深度的旅行。第259节说在某些梦实相的层面，你还没感知为物质的形式确实存在，看得见也摸得着。第277节强调，投射期间你打交道的是意识层面并不熟悉的环境与实相，但你对它们是有意识觉知的。第326节提醒梦里的同行者分好几种：也在投射的真人、死后犹存的人格，还有依你投射的程度正在别的层面或系统里过正常生活的人。第758节解释了为什么这些经验一回到白天就变成天堂一游：你拿熟悉的道具把非官方的资料装扮成认得的样子。第710节和第149节给了层面对照：在梦与其他实相层面，概念与它的象征被即刻经验到，感受与它外化的状况之间没有时间延迟，而梦意象在空间里的机动性远大于你。第183节收尾：梦里时间障碍可以大致放下，于是多出一块心灵空间等着被填。", "src": "第 219、259、277、326、758、710、149、183 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 219 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 259 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 277 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 326 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 758 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 710 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 149 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 183 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-096-e0966", "zh": "我们再次开始谈我们的片刻点。现在，这个出现在你们物质宇宙的片刻点，是这个广阔的现在较大部分的一个小小实现。在梦的状态，当自我从时间是一系列的片刻这种概念里解脱出来，那自己的其他部分可以旅行过这些片刻点，然后在这里，你会开始一趟和你的概念中的时间空间无关的、穿越深度的旅行。", "en": "We start once more with our moment point. For now this moment point which appears within your physical universe is but a small materialization of larger portions of the spacious present. In the dreaming state, when the ego is released from its idea of time as a series of moments, then other portions of the self can travel through these moment points, and you have here a journey through depths that have nothing to do with your （underline your） concept of time or space.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第219节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "219", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1046", "zh": "现在。在某些梦实相的层面上，你还没有感知它是物质的形式确实存在。它们是可以被看见，也可以被感知的。在某些梦中，你的确感知到它们。在梦实相之内，你可以接触到其他很多你平常不需要面对的实相。", "en": "Now. In certain levels of dream reality forms that you do not as yet perceive as physical, dfl exist. They can be seen and perceived. In certain dreams you do perceive them. Within dream reality you can come in contact with many other kinds of reality with which you do not ordinarily have to deal.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第259节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "259", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1060", "zh": "在投射期间，你正在打交道的是，你在意识层面上不熟悉的环境和实相。可是，在投射期间，你对它们是有意识觉知的。", "en": "During projection you are dealing with environments and realities with which you are not acquainted on a conscious level. Yet during projections you will be consciously aware of them.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第277节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "277", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1145", "zh": "在你的梦中，有些人将会是你认识的真人，他人也在投射中。其他人则是死后犹存的人格。在 某些情况下，根据你自己的投射程度，有些人会在其他层面或系统之内过着正常的生活。他们可能会也可能不会感知你。", "en": "Some of the people in your dreams will be actual people you know who are also projecting. Others will he survival personalities. In some cases according to your own level of projection, some will be going about their normal lives within other planes or systems. They may or may not perceive you.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第326节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "326", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2314", "zh": "因此，这些梦往往就像安排好的戏，在其中你已熟悉的道具来掩饰这种造访。当你经验到不同凡响的灵感闪现时，或感知其它非官方的资料时，这类的事常常发生。你迅速地试着使这种数据合乎常理。例如，一次进入实相其它层面的出体（out-of- body）经验，变成一次天堂之游。或直到现在未被认出的、你自己更大的本质的声音，变成了神、或宇宙人、或先知的声音。", "en": "So, often such dreams are like programmed dramas, in that you clothe such visitations in familiar props. The same sort of thing frequently occurs when you experience extraordinary flashes of inspiration, or perceive other unofficial data. Quickly you try to make sense of such material in usual terms. An out-of-body experience into another level of reality becomes a visit to heaven, for example; or the heretofore-unrecognized voice of your own greater identity becomes the voice of God, or a spaceman or prophet.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第758节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "758", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2108", "zh": "在梦境及在实相的某些其它层面里，概念及其象征即刻的被经验到。于是，在一个感受及其“外在化了的”状况之间没有时间的延迟，它自动被那个持有它的人以他熟悉并且觉得自然的不论什么方式经验到。心灵被示以它自己的观念，那些观念即刻反映在梦的情况以及马上就会解释的其它事件里。举例来说，如果在物质生活里，如果你梦想着或渴望着一幢新房子，那么，在这个理想实现之前可能要花些时间，虽然这样一个强烈意图将非常确定的带来其具体的实现。不过，在梦境里那同样的愿望可能导致这样一个房子的即刻创造，至少就你的梦中经验而言是如此。再次的，在愿望及其具体化之间没有时间的延迟。", "en": "In the dream state and in certain other levels of reality, ideas and their symbols are immediately experienced. There is no time lag, then, between a feeling and its “exteriorized” condition. It is automatically experienced in whatever form is familiar and natural to the one who holds it. The psyche is presented with its own concepts, which are instantly reflected in dream situations and other events that will be explained shortly. If you dream of or yearn for a new house in physical life, for instance, it may take some time before that ideal is realized, even though such a strong intent will most certainly bring about its physical fulfillment. The same desire in the dreaming state, however, may lead to the instant creation of such a house as far as your dream experience is concerned. Again, there is no time lag there between desire and its materialization.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第710节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "710", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0790", "zh": "梦中意象执行的这些行动当中，很多是肌肉的行动，身体的操纵。但这些行动也有很多是心智的操纵，或是美感的体现，甚至是美感的演出。这些梦意象绝对不是单一维度的虚构人物。就视角来说，它们的机动性在空间之内远远大过于你们自己。", "en": "Many of these actions performed by dream images are muscular ones, physical manipulations. But many of these actions are also mental manipulations, or esthetic realizations and even esthetic performances. These dream images are not one-dimensional, cardboard figures by any means. Their mobility in terms of perspectives and within space is far greater than your own.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0873", "zh": "这里也有电子上的意涵，非常重要，电子成分组成了情感经验，很容易在某些颜色氛围里头显示出来。在梦境中，内在经验并不像醒时状态下那样受限，所以可以大大摆脱时间上的障碍，因此有多余的心灵空间留给其他情感经验。", "en": "There are electrical connotations here also that are important, electrical components that compose the emotional experience, and that tend to show themselves in certain auras of color. Within the dreaming state however inner experience is not limited as it is in the waking condition, so that the time barrier can be largely dispensed with. There is an additional psychic space to be filled.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第183节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "183", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B09", "title": "通道常在，但有些方向天生难走", "note": "第575节先给一句容易忽略的话：任何一个人都能穿过这些层面而毫不为动、不知不觉，无所见地旅行过此地；资料在每一个被提到的意识层面都在，但要靠有意识的欲望或强烈的无意识欲望去把它找出来，不然那些礼物与潜能照旧没人认领。同节的另一半说有些层面天生自带阻碍，例如从你的宇宙投射进一个反物质宇宙是最困难的。第569节要紧地补上客观性：梦与接近人世的层面里个人发挥的余地确实极大，但这一切都发生在一个确切的、有它自己规则的环境里，那个环境的特性才让这些现象成为可能。第531节说所有意识之河之间都有相通的道路，你可以到我这边来，我也能到你那边去。第463节说所有层面之间都有不断的交互。第892节说在你们没认知的其他层面，你们与它们之间也有经常的沟通。第433节给了结果：多维度人格因此能够在各个层面建立接触，他们的关系里含有一种你所没有的信任。", "src": "第 575、569、531、463、892、433 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 575 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 569 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 531 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 463 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 892 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 433 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-096-e1552", "zh": "其实任何一个人都能经过这些层面而维持相当的不为所动及不知不觉，也能无所见地旅行过此地。个人的全盘性的目的与特性会决定他感知与了解的品质。所提及的资料在所说的每一个意识层面都有，但它必须透过有意识的欲望或强烈的无意识的欲望而被找出来。若非如此，那么可得的礼物与潜能就依然没被用到，没被争取到。", "en": "Now any individual can pass through these levels and remain relatively untouched and unaware, can travel through them unperceiving. The overall intentions and characteristics of the personality will determine the quality of perception and understanding. The material mentioned is available in each of the levels of consciousness given, but it must be sought out, either through conscious desire or strong unconscious desire. If it is not, then the gifts available and the potentials simply remain unused and unclaimed.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第575节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "575", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1567", "zh": "为此之故，你较不易向那些方向旅行。在有些层面里面有些天生固有的阻碍。举例来说，由你的宇宙投射到一个反物质宇宙是最困难的。即使你思想的电磁结构也会受到反面的影响，但理论上，从一个这种意识的邻接层面你却是可能投射过去的。", "en": "For this reason, you are much less apt to travel in those directions. In some there are built-in impediments. Even projection from your universe into a universe of antimatter is most difficult, for example. The electromagnetic makeup even of your thoughts would be adversely affected, and yet theoretically this is possible from one of these adjacent levels of consciousness.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第575节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "575", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1508", "zh": "可是，那时他们就在以之后从未再尝试的方式，努力画出内在实相的地图。在梦境与接近人世的一些其他存在层面里，在形相的创造及象征符号的卓越应用上，是真的有极大的个人的活动余地。但在另一方面来说，所有这些都在一个“客观的”确切环境里发生，那个环境具有使这种现象成为可能的特性——那么，那个活动场所拥有它自己的规则。“说法者”是熟习那些规则的，而常常当向导。有时他们在组织内工作，像在古埃及，他们透过庙宇工作而变得卷入了权力结构。不过，一般而言，他们是孤单得多的独行侠。", "en": "However, efforts were being made then to map inner reality in ways that have not been attempted since. It is true that in the dream state and in some other levels of existence close to your own, there is strong individual play in the creation of images, and a magnificent use of symbolism, but all of this takes place, again, in an “objective” definite environment, an environment whose characteristics make such phenomena possible — a field of activity, then, with its own rules. Now the Speakers are familiar with those rules, and often serve as guides. They have at times worked within organizations as in Egypt, where they worked through the temples and became involved with the power structures. As a rule, however, they are far more solitary.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第569节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "569", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1693", "zh": "用你们的话来说，很明显的，我就是这么一条“怪鱼”，由意识流的深处游来，察看你们的生存空间。由此可见，在所有的意识河流之间皆有着可以相通的道路，也就是说在所有象征性心灵河流中皆有孔道，你可以到我这边来，我也可以到你那边去。", "en": "Now I am obviously such a one in your terms, swimming up through other dimensions of reality and observing a dimension of existence that is yours rather than my own. There are, therefore, channels that exist between all these streams of consciousness, all these symbolic rivers of psychological and psychic experience, and there are journeys that can be made from my dimension as well as yours.", "source": "时空之外 · 第531节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "531", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1314", "zh": "在所有层面上都有不断的交互。我会试着跟你们解释得更清楚。也要记住，按你们的说法，那个看似独立的被感知事件及其性质，会因你自己的知觉而改变。", "en": "There are constant interchanges on all levels. I will try to explain this to you more clearly. Remember also in your terms that the seemingly independent perceived event and its nature is changed and altered by your own perception of it.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第463节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "463", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2520", "zh": "在其它你们并没认知的层面，它们和你们之间也有经常的沟通，以致在每个物种和其环境之间有无止境的相互作用。", "en": "There is also constant communication between them and you at other levels than those you recognize, so that there is an unending interplay between each species and its environment.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第892节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "892", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1272", "zh": "因此，多维度人格能够在各个层面建立接触。他们的关系里含有一种你们所没有的信任。他们有许多的共识领域敞开着。", "en": "Multidimensional personalities can therefore establish contact at various levels. Their relationships involve a trust that yours do not have. They have many areas of agreement open.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第433节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "433", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B10", "title": "层面不是幻造：各有各的规则，也守同一套基本律", "note": "怕的是把这套坐标读成爱怎么想就怎么想。第704节先立底线：再怎样的伪装模式也必须遵循内在宇宙的基本规则并反映它们，哪怕是以扭曲的方式；价值扩展因此变成再投胎、演化与成长，内在宇宙其余的基本定律在每个层面都被遵循，从最微小到最巨大。第698节说没有一个实相系统是封闭的，你以为的官方经验并不是独自悬在时空里，而是与你认不出的另一些线段交织着；意识心在醒时必须聚焦在你们称为实相的那个集中点上，但它本来也配备得足以在其他实相层面多少指挥你。第798节给了最宽容的一句：内在的领域足够大，能在一个层面容纳矛盾，因为在另一个层面它们看起来完全不矛盾。第5节说相互关联的场与层面连接着所有各种生命，不是靠某一个生物或灵性的系统支撑，而是在它存在的每一个想象的点上支撑它；没有封闭的系统。第17节是最干净的一条：每一个世界都是另一个的一部分，并没有不相连接的；并没有一个心理的或心灵的地方或空间，让那些世界在那里彼此分开地存在。第519节还顺手举了个参照：在赛斯所在的那个层次，我不是我的意识、意识只是被我运用的一种东西，是常识。", "src": "第 704、698、798、5、17、519 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 704 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 698 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 798 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 5 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 17 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 519 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-096-e2088", "zh": "然而，即使是这种伪装模式也必须遵循内在宇宙的基本规则，并且反映它们，即使是一种扭曲了的方式。价值扩展因而变成再投胎、演化及成长，因而，内在宇宙所有其他的基本定律也在每个层面上被遵循，而由最细微到最巨大的每一个阶层反映出来。", "en": "Yet even these camouflage patterns must follow the basic rules of the inner universe, and reflect them, even if in a distortive manner. So does value expansion become reincarnation and evolution and growth. So are all the other basic laws of the inner universe followed on every plane, and reflected from the most minute to the most gigantic spectrum.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第704节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "704", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2048", "zh": "在这本书里我先前说过，你们所知的世界升自基本的不可预测性，然后重要意义才由其中浮出。没有一个实相系统是封闭的，那么，你称之为你官方经验的那特定一串的可能性行动并不只是悬空在空间与时间里——它与你们并不认识的其他这种“行动股”交织在一起。在醒时状态，意识心必须颇为单一的聚焦在你们称为实相的那特定的集中点上，只因为如此的话，它才能在俗世生活里适当的指挥你的活动，不过，当它不需要担负明确的存活责任时，它也有相当的配备而多少能在其他的实相层面里指挥你。", "en": "I said earlier in this book that the world you know arises from basic unpredictability, from which significances then emerge. 4 No system of reality is closed. The particular string of probable actions that you call your official experience does not just dangle, then, out in space and time — it interweaves with other such strands that you do not recognize. In the waking state the conscious mind must focus rather exclusively upon that one particular point of concentration that you call reality, simply so that it can direct your activities properly in temporal life. It is quite equipped, however, also to direct you to some extent in other levels of reality when it is not needed for specific survival duties.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第698节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "698", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2413", "zh": "口授：当然，你的下一个问题很容易猜到，因你会想知道那“内在的”世界的起源。我曾说外在世界乃是从它浮露出来的——而此地我们必须与我们珍视的客观性说再见，而进入一个精神领域，在其中可以明白矛盾并非错误；一个足够大到在一个层面能包容矛盾的内在领域，因为在另一个层面它们看来完全不矛盾。", "en": "Dictation: Your next question is easy to anticipate, of course, for you will want to know the origin of that “interior” universe from which I have said the exterior one ever emerges — and here we must part company with treasured objectivity, and enter instead a mental domain, in which it is seen that contradictions are not errors; an inner domain large enough to contain contradictions at one level, for at another level they are seen to be no contradictions at all.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第798节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "798", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2626", "zh": "相互关联的场（field）或层面（planes）连结着所有各种的生命，并非经由，比如说，一个系统——一个生物的或灵性的系统——支持着它，却是在它存在的每个可想象的点支持它。你并非被给予一定份量的刚才提到的能量。「新」能量到处可得。再次的，并没有关闭的系统。再次的，环境是有意义且活生生的，在你身体的所有各部分和环境的所有各部分之间，有经常的沟通。", "en": "Fields, or p-l-a-n-e-s (spelled) of interrelatedness connect all kinds of life, supporting it not through, say, just one system — a biological one or a spiritual one — but at every conceivable point of its existence. You are not just given so much energy, in those terms earlier mentioned. “New” energy is everywhere available. Again, there are no closed systems. Again, the environment is conscious and alive. There are constant communications between all portions of your body and all portions of the environment.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第5节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "5", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2644", "zh": "因为世界是如此组成的，每一个世界都是另一个的一部分，并没有不相连接的。并没有一个心理的或心灵的地方或空间，在那儿那些世界彼此分开地存在，因此，你不能说，一个世界是比另一个进化得较高。", "en": "For the worlds are so composed that each one is a part of each other one, and there is no disconnecting. There is no place or space, psychological, psychic, where those worlds exist apart from each other, so you cannot say that one is more highly evolved than another.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第17节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "17", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1655", "zh": "它运用无数的知觉方式，而且掌管多种不同的意识形态。你们对灵魂的观念只局限于三度空间。灵魂能改变它意识的焦点，并且能像你们用大脑指挥眼睛看东西一样来运用意识。在我目前所存在的层次中，这是一种常识，但是下面这种说法也许令人觉得奇怪：我并非我的意识，我的意识只是被我运用的一种东西而已，这一点适用于每一个这本书的读者，只是各位也许不知道这个潜藏的真相。所以灵魂——或是全我——比意识包涵之范围要广、要多。", "en": "It utilizes numberless methods of perception, and it has at its command many other kinds of consciousness. Your idea of the soul is indeed limited by your three-dimensional concepts. The soul can change the focus of its consciousness, and uses consciousness as you use the eyes in your head. Now in my level of existence I am simply aware of the fact, strange as it may seem, that I am not my consciousness. My consciousness is an attribute to be used by me. This applies to each of the readers of this book, even though the knowledge may be hidden. Soul or entity, then, is more than consciousness.", "source": "时空之外 · 第519节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "519", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B11", "title": "换掉这张坐标，跟你有什么关系", "note": "第743节几乎是直接下命令：忘掉人家曾告诉你关于时间与空间是怎么一回事的那些话，拒绝接受那局限你自己自然天性的幅度之概念，未知的实相就是你。第898节解释了为什么这值得做：你生前主观地活着，死后也会主观地活着，现在只是透过你称为清醒这种专门化的意识状态来诠释，而你只承认落入某些时空坐标里的经验为真实，你更大的实相在那些坐标之外。第512节给出代价：你对实相本质的观念多狭窄，自我就多不遗余力地把你留在多小的世界里；直觉与创造本能一被放开，它们就会把较大维度的知识与体会带给这个最受物质困限的部分。第515节举赛斯那边为例：他们没有生长的花草，但心理性质那强烈密集的力量自己形成活动的新空间，而这种能力不是他们独有，那是你本来的遗产。第558节落到安心处：你不可能被一个你不了解的恐惧从实相的一个层面追赶到另一个层面。", "src": "第 743、898、512、515、558 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 743 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 898 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 512 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 515 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 558 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-096-e2248", "zh": "忘掉人家曾告诉你关于时间与空间是怎么一回事的那些话，拒绝接受那局限你自己自然天性的幅度之概念。再说一次，未知的实相就是“你”。", "en": "Forget what you have been told about time and space. Refuse to accept ideas that limit the dimensions of your own natural being. Again, the unknown reality is what you are.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第743节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "743", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2536", "zh": "在你生前你是主观的“活着”；在你死后你也将会主观的活着。你的主观生活现在是被透过你称为清醒的那种专门化的意识状态来诠释，在其中，你只承受将落入某些时空坐标里的经验为真实，你的更大的实相存在于那些坐标之外，而宇宙的实相也一样。（停顿。）你们为你们自己创造生活，当你一边走一边改变它们，就像一位作者可能改变一本书，变更那些环境及改变那些情节。那作家只知道它创造了，而并没了解创造力赖以发生的自发性秩序，那过程发生在意识的另一个层面。", "en": "You are subjectively “alive” before your birth. You will be subjectively alive after your death. Your subjective life is now interpreted through the specialized state of consciousness that you call the waking one, in which you recognize as real only experience that falls within certain space and time coordinates. Your greater reality exists outside those coordinates, and so does the reality of the universe. (Pause.) You create lives for yourselves, changing them as you go along, as a writer might change a book, altering the circumstances, changing the plots. The writer only knows that he or she creates without understanding the spontaneous order with which the creativity happens. The processes occur at another level of consciousness (underlined).", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第898节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "898", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1636", "zh": "如果你对实相的本质观念狭窄，那么你的自我即会不遣余力的助你自限于你仅能接受的狭小世界中。反之，若是你的情形正好相反，那么你的领悟力及创造力都可得到释放，进而与高层次空间接触，为你那饱受物质困限的部分带来一些体会与知识。", "en": "If you have a limited conception of the nature of reality, then your ego will do its best to keep you in the small enclosed area of your accepted reality. If, on the other hand, your intuitions and creative instincts are allowed freedom, then they communicate some knowledge of greater dimensions to this most physically oriented portion of your personality.", "source": "时空之外 · 第512节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "512", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1646", "zh": "我们对我们的环境赋予更大的创造秉赋，这点很难解释。举例说：我们没有生长的花草，但是我们那本然强烈密集的心灵力量却能形成活动的新空间。如果你在三度空间中画一幅画，那副画必然是在一个平面上，仅能有限度的暗示三度空间的感受，而不能将三度空间置入画中。但是在我们的环境中，我们能真实的创造出任何一种我们想要表达的空间效果。这种能力并非只有我们才具有，你们本来也具有。在此书后面几章中，你们将会看到，你们也可以在意识的其他状态中（如梦中）运用你们自己的内在感官，运用你们多重空间性的能力，你们可以运用的频度要比你们自以为可能的次数还多。", "en": "We endow the elements of our environment with an even greater creativity that is difficult to explain. We do not have flowers that grow, for example. But the intensity, the condensed psychic strength of our psychological natures forms new dimensions of activity. If you paint a picture within three-dimensional existence, then the painting must be on a flat surface, merely hinting at the complete three-dimensional experience that you cannot insert into it. In our environment, however, we could actually create whatever dimensional effects we desired. All of these abilities are not ours alone. They are your heritage. As you will see later in this book, you exercise your own inner senses, and multidimensional abilities, more frequently than it might seem, in other states of consciousness than the normal, waking one.", "source": "时空之外 · 第515节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "515", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1493", "zh": "按照你的了解，你作你自己的决定。你不可能被一个你不了解的恐惧由实相的一个层面追逐到另一个层面。你在此生也不能被来自你早年或所谓的前世的恐惧所威胁，除非你如此彻底的相信恐惧的本质而允许你自己被它征服。你的每一个人格都可以从实相奇迹似的库存中，自由的接受与发展那些你想要的经验与感情，而摒弃那些你不要的。", "en": "The decision is your own according to your understanding. You cannot be hounded from one level of reality to another by a fear that you do not understand. You cannot be threatened in this life by fears from your early childhood, or by so-called past existences, unless you so thoroughly believe in the nature of fear that you allow yourselves to be conquered by it. Each of your personalities are free to accept and develop, from the miraculous banks of reality, those experiences and emotions that you want, and to reject those you do not want.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第558节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "558", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [{"id": "q-concept-096-e0046", "zh": "至于你今天早上谈到艺术的随笔，非常好，我很赞赏。你已经开始用比较宽广的新观念来思考。你的绘画就是在画板或纸上的固化感觉——在物质宇宙明显可见，因此容易受到宇宙法则的影响。同样的，宇宙本身在你们的层面上也是物质具体化的感觉，只不过它的维度多过于一幅素描或画而已。然而，在线条和颜色，以及形式和内容之外，画中还另外有个超越一般人通常能辨识的维度，那就是你已经很巧妙形容的“感觉的固化”。你有了行动，这你自己也说过。首先你有捕捉并固化画中线条、形式和内容等等的行动，然后你以观看者的角度看着画，这时感觉又变成行动，从画中出来，进入观看者的知觉。", "en": "As to your jottings this morning concerning art, very good, I commend you. You are already beginning to think in new and divider concepts. As your paintings are solidified feeling on board or paper, apparent in the physical universe and therefore vulnerable to the laws of that universe, so is the universe itself on your plane physical materialized feeling, only with more dimension than a drawing or a painting. There is however also an extra dimension in a painting than people usually recognize, beside the lines and color and form and content, which are as you said so aptly feeling solidified. You have the action of which you also spoke. First you have the action of the lines, form and content and so forth, caught and solidified, then as an observer looks at a painting feeling is again motion moving out from the painting into the beholder’s perception.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第14节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "14", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0138", "zh": "这里你们必须记住，时间是伪装模式的一部分。现在外在的视觉感官似乎混淆空间，而且使用你们的眼睛好像可以克服一部分的距离。也就是说，你不必走这短短的距离，才看得到某个特定空间所涉及的什么东西。", "en": "You must remember here that time is part of the camouflage pattern. Now the outer sense of sight would seem to confound space, and seemingly conquer a portion of distance by using your eyes. That is, you do not necessarily have to walk a short distance in order to see what is in the particular space involved.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第20节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "20", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0161", "zh": "我只不过刚开始探讨这一点，但这件事情是极为重要的。每个离开你们层面的人都已经尽其所能在你们的层面发展到极限了。但是就像在你们的生活中，某些环境比较容易激励一些人实现他们的才能，而对另一些人来说似乎阻碍了他们特有才能的发展，所以有些人在你们层面扩展了他们的能力；而另一些则在你们层面上完成得相当不佳，但在其他层面则出乎意料地扩展。", "en": "I have only begun to go into this, but this matter is extremely important. Everyone who has left your plane has developed as far as he can on your plane. But as in your life certain environments tend to encourage some people in the realization of their talents, and seem to hinder others in the development of their peculiar talents, so some personalities expand in their capabilities on your plane; and some who do rather poorly on your plane expand surprisingly on other planes.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第23节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "23", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0345", "zh": "这些伪装概念的真实性与实用性，与物质的伪装模式比起来，只可能有过之而无不及。它们也使你们可以操纵，当然也可以让你们躲掉或挡掉直接的实相经验，因为在你们层面中，你们是无法处理这些经验的。", "en": "These camouflage ideas are as real and as useful, if not more so, than physical camouflage patterns. They also enable you to manipulate, and they of course also serve to hide you from or shield you from direct reality experiences which you cannot handle on your plane.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第41节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "41", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0436", "zh": "我也说过，所谓的空间旅行，将必然脱离它当前与载具的关系。人们将会发现，内在感官是你们唯一一种进行这类旅行的持久方法。", "en": "I have also said that space travel, so-called, will of necessity deviate from its present concern with vehicles. It will be discovered that the inner senses represent your only longlasting method of such travel.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第49节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "49", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0488", "zh": "但是，就像心智对树来说，代表，而它也确实代表，动作和兴奋，意识在匆匆穿越所谓空间的细胞与分子时，也代表焕然一新的经验和短暂而崭新的满足感。", "en": "But as the mind represents, and it does, motion and excitement to the trees, so would the consciousness, as it rustled through the cells and molecules of so-called space, represent refreshing experience and momentary new satisfactions.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第55节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "55", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0574", "zh": "死亡在你们层面上，和其他事情一样，其实是这样一个点上的一次抵达。这一点我们以后再更仔细地讨论。", "en": "Death on your plane is actually, among other things, an arrival at such a point. This will be discussed more fully later.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第66节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "66", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e0707", "zh": "现在。和你们的房东、他太太以及他死去的父亲有关的经验，确有其事；但有一个我应该想要用来当例子，做一场颇为冗长的讨论，谈谈直接肇因于最近几节的问题。也就是，和所谓死亡那一刻之后的肉体形象存活，以及人格各部分的物质层面有关的问题。", "en": "Now. The experience involving your landlord, his wife and his deceased father, was a legitimate one; but one that I should like to use as an example for a rather long discussion of questions directly resulting from some recent sessions. That is, the question as to the survival of the physical image after the point of so-called death, and the lingering about the physical plane of portions of the personality.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第100节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "100", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1019", "zh": "现在。他理所当然地认为梦地点不存在于物质空间之内。", "en": "Now. He has taken it for granted that dream locations do not exist within physical space.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第244节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "244", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1081", "zh": "杰出的艺术作品也为观察者重新创造他自己的内在经验，而他或许不曾察觉。就像你知道的，绘画有动作，可是画作本身不会动。这个概念也许可以帮助你从强度来了解经验，以及投射或意识的活动，不一定牵涉到空间。", "en": "The excellent work of art recreates for the observer inner experience of his own also, of which he has perhaps never been aware. As you know, paintings have motion, yet the painting itself does not move. This idea perhaps will help you to understand experience in terms of intensity, and projections, or the movement of consciousness, without necessarily any involvement with space.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第287节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "287", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e1478", "zh": "转世经验是“自己”这个架构的一部分，是活生生的心灵的多次元实相的一面。因此，这些经验不只会在梦境，也会在其他的活动层面里反映出来。", "en": "Reincarnational experiences are a part of the framework of the self, a facet of the multidimensional reality of the living psyche. These experiences will, therefore, be reflected not only in the dream state, but in other layers of activity.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第556节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "556", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2488", "zh": "如我大半的读者所知，我并不宣称我现在是一个具有肉体的人。（停顿。）但我的确宣称，在另一个存在的层面，我有个独立的实相。我的身份来源看似奇怪，只因你们对自己的来源了解得这么少。今晚我开始这本书，我已给过书名，而珍•罗伯兹（在十二天前）已能感知部分将被包括在此的某些话题。不过，到现在为止，具体的东西只有罗勃•伯兹写下我说的这些话的纸张。", "en": "As most of my readers know, I make no claims of now having a physical personhood. (Pause.) I do claim an independent reality at another level of existence. My status and origins seem strange only because you have understood so little about your own origins. I am beginning this book this evening. I have already given the title, and at another level of consciousness Jane Roberts was able (12 days ago, for example) to perceive some glimpses of some of the subject matter that will be included here. So far, however, physically there is only the page of paper upon which Robert Butts is writing down these words I speak.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第881节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "881", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2600", "zh": "某一种方式，你在那个层面“踏入那事件”。你接受或排除它为一个可能性。你做某种调整，或许改变物定的细节，但你踏入并且变成那内在过程的一部分——在事件变成一个确定的实质确实之前，影响它的形状、大小及性质。", "en": "In a certain fashion you “step into the event” at that level. You accept or reject it as a probability. You make certain adjustments, perhaps altering particular details, but you step into and become part of the inner processes—affecting, say, the shape or size or nature of the event before it becomes a definite physical actuality.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第932节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "932", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2624", "zh": "在你的梦里，你相当清楚地看到，在物质实相与神奇的次元之间的门坎，物质实相的源头是在神奇的次元里。你被示以——或给你自己看——两者之间不同的规则或假设。那只狗想吃食物的欲望，引它神奇地穿门进来，因为自然生物的欲望是以一种与你们对工作的概念完全无关的「轻易」被满足的。我想要做的是，引介一种不同的工作观念——非常有价值的、重要的工作，那是在另一个层面，并且以另一种方式执行的。", "en": "Now in your dream, you were quite clearly seeing the threshold between physical reality and the magical dimension in which that physical reality has its source. You were being shown — or showing yourself — the difference in the rules or assumptions between the two. The dog’s desire for food led him to walk magically through the door, for the desires of the natural creature are satisfied (pause) with an ease that has nothing to do with your ideas of work. What I am getting at is the introduction of the concepts of a different kind of work — very valuable, vital work that is performed at another level and in a different fashion.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第4节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "4", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-096-e2676", "zh": "不过，在所有的例子里，价值完成、表达和创意的需要对生命是如此重要，以致当这些受到威胁时，生命本身至少暂时减弱了。与生俱来地，每个人的确了解，有死后的生命，而在某些例子里，这些人领悟到，的确是时候了，是搬到另一个实相层面，去经历死亡而再次开始另一个全新世界的时候了。", "en": "In all cases, however, the need for value fulfillment, expression, and creativity are so important to life that when these are threatened, life itself is at least momentarily weakened. Innately, each person does realize that there is life after death, and in some instances such people realize that it is indeed time to move to another level of reality, to die and set out again with another brand-new world.", "source": "健康之道 · 第11节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "11", "only_en": false}], "books": [{"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 10}, {"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 9}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 8}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 8}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 7}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 7}, {"name": "时空之外", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 5}, {"name": "未知的实相卷二", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 3}, {"name": "未知的实相卷一", "count": 3}, {"name": "神奇之道", "count": 3}, {"name": "健康之道", "count": 2}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 2}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 2}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 2}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 2}], "span": [1963, 1984], "stats": {"blocks": 11, "quotes": 84, "reading": 15, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 1}};
